      ":question/problem": "Let $R = [1, 3] \\cdot [2, 4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 2x + 3y$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, \u2026, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, \u2026, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = \u2211_(i = 1)^(m)\u2211_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAA\u0394x_{i}\u0394y_{j}$\nwhere $\u0394x_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $\u0394y_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"
